> In twenty ten, the number of state-based armed conflicts documented around the world stood at around thirty, having progressively fallen since the break-up of the Soviet Union. The trend has now reversed. Between twenty ten and twenty twenty, the number nearly doubled to fifty-six, as did the number of conflict deaths. This doubling can also be seen in the numbers of refugees and other forcibly displaced people, which rose from forty-one million in twenty ten to eighty-two point four million in twenty twenty.
